From aabe0bb427fa2e21be55ea031c2b80a5107b28df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:19:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 184/193] urltest: retry a round with a URL that answered
 through the member

The retry of a round took the next URL of the list. A server whose hoster blocks two
operators that are neighbours in the list failed the URL of the round and its retry in one
round of each cycle: unavailable, and the group left it for that round (on the stand: 21
switches an hour, 85 % of the time on the fastest server, with gstatic and cp.cloudflare
blocked through it).

- The history keeps, per member and URL, whether the last test with the URL answered.
- The retry takes the first URL after the one of the round that answered through the
  member last time, the next one when none did. Still two tests a round at most: a server
  that is down is found as before. The URL of the round still goes round the list, so a
  blocked URL is tested again in its round.
- The one test that confirms a member whose connections fail takes the first URL, from the
  URL of the round on, that answered through it last time: a URL its server cannot reach
  no longer calls a working member down.
- Only a minority of URLs is passed over: when more than half of them did not answer
  through the member at their last test, the retry is the next URL and the confirmation the
  URL of the round, as before. A server that reaches one operator of five is not kept
  available by that one.
- Tests cut short by the end of a round, and tests the Clash API asks for with its own URL,
  are not kept.
